    "content": "Sasaram Set for Mega Rail Leap! ₹7 Billion North Junction to Connect Three Major Rail Lines and Power Bihar’s Industrial Future A New Rail Identity Rises in Sasaram Imagine stepping into a city that is no longer just a stop—but a strategic rail gateway of eastern India. That transformation has already begun in Sasaram, where a massive ₹7 billion railway project is reshaping its destiny. Near Karmdihari village, just five kilometers from the district headquarters, the upcoming Sasaram North Junction is taking shape at remarkable speed. Moreover, this ambitious infrastructure push promises to redefine railway connectivity in Bihar. As a result, Sasaram is set to gain national visibility in India’s rail network. This development is not just about platforms and tracks. Instead, it is about mobility, economic opportunity, and long-term regional growth. ₹7 Billion Investment: What’s Being Built? The Indian Railways has launched this high-impact project with a strong infrastructure focus. The new junction will feature two modern 700-meter platforms equipped with sheds and footbridges. Additionally, engineers are constructing two rail flyovers, one Rail Flyover Overbridge (RFO), and one Road Over Rail (ROR) bridge. Importantly, this junction will connect three major rail corridors: Son Nagar–Japla Line Gaya–Howrah Line Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyay–Delhi Main Line The Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyay",
