    "content": "₹574 Crore Boost: Bihar to Build World-Class Sports Stadium in Punpun Bihar is sprinting towards a new sporting era! With a massive ₹574 crore cabinet approval, Punpun in Patna district is set to welcome a world-class sports stadium. This investment is not just about infrastructure—it is about igniting dreams, fueling talent, and giving Bihar’s youth a stage to shine in national and international arenas. A Bold Step for Sports in Bihar The Bihar cabinet has cleared funds for acquiring 100 acres of land in Dumri village, Punpun block, to build this ambitious sports stadium. According to Arvind Kumar Choudhary, Additional Chief Secretary, Cabinet Secretariat Department, the project aims to inspire greater participation in sports and strengthen Bihar’s growing reputation in the athletic sector. Such developments not only bring infrastructure but also hope. They create opportunities for young athletes to train, compete, and represent Bihar on the global stage. Cricket in Focus: Rajgir’s International Stadium Alongside the Punpun project, the cabinet also gave its nod for a landmark decision in Bihar Cricket. The Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) will now vest rights in the Bihar Cricket Association (BCA) to maintain the upcoming international cricket stadium at Rajgir, Nalanda. This move ensures that Bihar’s cricket ecosystem grows under proper management while offering ",
