    "content": "Bihar Creates History: Darbhanga’s Arvind Achal Becomes the First International Cricket Umpire from the State Bihar’s Proud Moment on the Global Cricket Map If someone asks you, “Who is Bihar’s first international cricket umpire?” you finally have an answer that fills hearts with pride — Darbhanga’s Arvind Achal. For the first time in history, Bihar’s name shines on the global cricket stage. Arvind, from Makaranda village in Manigachi block of Darbhanga, has earned his place in the International Cricket Council’s (ICC) Development Umpire Panel. This milestone is more than a personal success. It marks a historic moment for Bihar and its cricketing dreams. The Long Road of Patience and Passion Arvind’s story is built on 25 years of dedication. He started from dusty playgrounds in Bihar and slowly advanced to domestic matches. With every game, he carved out his space in a field where recognition is rare. Unlike many youngsters who dreamed of playing for India with bat or ball, he chose umpiring. This path looked less glamorous, but it was equally significant. His focus stayed on discipline, fairness, and preserving the spirit of cricket rather than chasing personal fame. The Breakthrough: From Darbhanga to Estonia The breakthrough came when the ICC selected him to officiate international matches. His debut happened in Tallinn, Estonia, during T20 internationals between Switzerland",
