    "content": "“Muzaffarpur Wushu Girls Shine! Bihar’s Pride at Khelo India State League 2025” Muzaffarpur roars with glory as its Wushu warriors emerge overall champions at the Khelo India State Wushu League 2025 in Patna. The two-day event turned into a celebration of skill, discipline, and determination, with Muzaffarpur players bagging medals across every category. Bihar’s Wushu League at Patna STC The championship was held from 17 to 18 August 2025 at SAI STC, Rajendranagar, Patna. Organized jointly by the Bihar Wushu Association and Patna Wushu Association, the league witnessed the participation of over 250 women athletes from different districts of Bihar. The opening ceremony welcomed dignitaries like Veena Gupta (former District Governor, Lions Club Patna), Dr. Amulya Kumar Singh (President, Bihar Wushu Association), Dr. Sanjay Srivastava (Vice Chairman, Bihar Wushu Association), Someshwar Rao Chaman (SAI STC Centre Incharge), and other senior officials. Muzaffarpur Claims Top Spot On the closing day, Muzaffarpur Wushu Association stood tall with 99 points, securing the first position. Buxar Wushu Association followed with 53 points, while Patna Wushu Association managed third place with 41 points. The victories ignited celebrations in Muzaffarpur as young champions received applause from across Bihar. Star Medal Winners from Muzaffarpur The highlight of the championship was the stell",
