    "summary": "“Why Most LinkedIn Pages Die in 100 Days — And How Bihar Say Became a 13K-Strong Community Instead” From Zero to 13K: The Bihar Say Story Most LinkedIn pages vanish in less than 100 days. Yet, Bihar Say didn’t just su...",
    "content": "“Why Most LinkedIn Pages Die in 100 Days — And How Bihar Say Became a 13K-Strong Community Instead” From Zero to 13K: The Bihar Say Story Most LinkedIn pages vanish in less than 100 days. Yet, Bihar Say didn’t just survive — it thrived. Over two years, we have grown into a 13,000-strong global community. I’ve watched many Bihar-focused pages start with excitement, chase viral posts, and disappear quickly. Clearly, the intent fades, consistency drops, and purpose blurs. This is the difference between building a page and building a community. A Passion, Not a Project When we launched Bihar Say, it wasn’t a campaign or side hustle. Instead, it was a passion project with zero funding, no PR, and no shortcuts. One belief drove us:👉 Bihar deserves a space where stories of progress, pride, and positivity can thrive — without bias. Lesson 1: Patience Builds Trust Community building rewards sincerity more than speed. Engagement was low at first, yet our intent remained strong. Gradually, patience turned into trust. People began to notice authenticity over fleeting trends. This trust kept us motivated. Lesson 2: Purpose Over Popularity Virality fades quickly, but purpose lasts. Therefore, we avoided becoming just another meme or news page. Instead, our goal was clear: change Bihar’s narrative through authentic, apolitical storytelling. Consequently, our audience stayed and grew. Lesson ",
