    "content": "“Sumant Sinha of ReNew Power – Bihar’s ₹3,000 Crore Green Energy Visionary” “Bihar has always produced leaders — but in today’s era, one man from the state is powering not just homes, but India’s clean energy future: Sumant Sinha.” Who is Sumant Sinha? Born into a family known for public service, Sumant Sinha is the son of Yashwant Sinha, India’s former Finance Secretary and Union Minister. Unlike his father, who chose politics and administration, Sumant carved a different path. He entered the corporate world with a focus on energy, finance, and business leadership. Educated at IIT Delhi and Columbia University, Sumant developed a rare mix of technical knowledge and financial expertise. This combination later became the backbone of his success in the renewable energy industry. Before starting his own venture, he held senior positions at Aditya Birla Group and Suzlon Energy, gaining both global exposure and sectoral insight. However, it was his entrepreneurial leap that changed everything. ReNew Power – Sumant Sinha’s Green Revolution In 2011, Sumant Sinha founded ReNew Power with a clear mission: to make renewable energy mainstream in India. At a time when many companies still relied on coal and oil, his idea looked risky. But his vision was strong — India needed clean power for sustainable growth. Today, ReNew Power has grown into India’s largest renewable energy company. With",
