    "content": "पटना की सैर अब होगी और भी खास: Double Decker Bus Ride on JP Ganga Path Patna just unlocked a new way to enjoy its beauty. Picture yourself on the upper deck of a stylish bus, the wind in your hair, while the Ganga flows beside you. This is no longer imagination—it’s the Double Decker Bus service on JP Ganga Path, and it promises an experience like never before. A Fresh Tourism Chapter for Patna The Bihar Tourism Department is turning JP Ganga Path into a major attraction. Now, visitors can travel from Tourism Ghat to Kangan Ghat along the scenic 15-kilometer stretch. Today, Tourism Minister Shri Raju Kumar Singh inaugurated this service with great enthusiasm. At the same time, Bihar State Tourism Development Corporation (BSTDC) Managing Director Shri Nand Kishore welcomed him and highlighted the importance of this initiative. Comfort Meets Innovation This isn’t just a bus—it’s an experience crafted for tourists. The double decker has 40 seats: 20 comfortable air-conditioned seats below and 20 open-air seats above. In addition, the bus offers modern facilities like a washroom and a fridge, which make the ride both practical and enjoyable. Moreover, a professional guide joins every journey. They share stories about Patna’s famous landmarks, ensuring travelers connect deeply with each destination. Iconic Sights Along the Route The journey covers several cultural and historical hig",
