    "title": "PM Modi Praises Nalanda Weaver Naveen Kumar in ‘Mann Ki Baat’",
    "summary": "“PM Modi’s Shoutout Turns a Bihar Weaver into a National Symbol of Hope” How a small village in Nalanda became the epicentre of pride, progress, and possibilities. When the Nation Listens, a Village Rises For the weav...",
    "content": "“PM Modi’s Shoutout Turns a Bihar Weaver into a National Symbol of Hope” How a small village in Nalanda became the epicentre of pride, progress, and possibilities. When the Nation Listens, a Village Rises For the weavers of Nepura, a village tucked away in Nalanda district of Bihar, July 28 wasn’t just another Sunday. It was the day Prime Minister Narendra Modi, during his popular radio program Mann Ki Baat, praised local weaver Naveen Kumar for embracing tradition while innovating with technology. The recognition struck a deep chord. Children cheered, women smiled, and elders teared up. “This moment isn’t just about me,” Naveen said. “It’s about every weaver who stayed committed to the loom.” A Joy That Echoed Through Every Thread The impact of PM Modi’s words was immediate. Families in Nepura replayed the radio broadcast with pride. Streets lit up with smiles and celebration. Until now, many weavers felt invisible in national conversations. However, this public praise changed that in an instant. “We finally feel seen,” said one elder. “It gives us strength to continue and innovate.” Blending Ancestral Craft With Modern Tools Naveen Kumar, who also leads the Nepura Primary Weavers Cooperative Committee, is not only carrying forward his family tradition—he’s upgrading it. Earlier, artisans worked on pit looms, which required them to sit in sunken pits. Thanks to the Ministry of",
