    "summary": "“Devotion Reaches New Heights: 32-Foot Mahadev Statue in Patna Becomes Sawan’s Biggest Spiritual Magnet” Bhakti at Its Peak: Mahadev Statue Becomes the Talk of Patna “Jahan bhakti ho gehri, wahan chamatkaar bhi zaroor...",
    "content": "“Devotion Reaches New Heights: 32-Foot Mahadev Statue in Patna Becomes Sawan’s Biggest Spiritual Magnet” Bhakti at Its Peak: Mahadev Statue Becomes the Talk of Patna “Jahan bhakti ho gehri, wahan chamatkaar bhi zaroori hai!”That’s exactly what Samkuda village, in Patna’s Masaurhi block, witnessed on the first Monday of Sawan. A sea of devotees gathered around a 32-foot statue of Lord Shiva, their eyes filled with faith and hearts full of hope. The energy was electrifying. Conch shells echoed, incense wafted through the air, and chants of “Har Har Mahadev” rang out from every corner. Born During Lockdown, Now Bihar’s Tallest Shiva Statue The artist behind this divine marvel, Sanjeev Kumar, didn’t plan to make headlines. A native of Samastipur and a student at Patna Art College, Sanjeev got stranded in Samkuda during the COVID-19 lockdown. Rather than sit idle, he picked up his tools and followed his heart. He started with the idea of a small statue. But as time passed and faith deepened, the sculpture grew — eventually reaching 32 feet in height. “People travel from far-off districts just to get a glimpse. Many say their wishes come true here,” Sanjeev shares, his tone humble yet proud. This towering Mahadev now draws both devotees and tourists. It’s not just a statue. It’s a symbol of resilience, faith, and Bihar’s deep-rooted spiritual strength. From a Shivling to a Spiritual ",
